{title: 428 - Sweet By and By}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #428 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 428}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em/B]There’s a [G/D]land [D]that is [D7/C]fairer [C]than [G]day,
[G/B]And by faith we can [Bm]see it afar;
[Em/B]For the Father [G/D]waits over the [D7/C]way
[C]To prepare [G/B]us a dwelling place [D7/C]there.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D7/A]In the sweet in [Em/B]the sweet
[Em]By and [D]by by and by,
[D]We shall meet [D7]on that beautiful shore;
[D7]In the [G/D]sweet in the sweet
[D]By and by by [G]and by
[C/G]We shall [G]meet on that [D7/C]beautiful [Em/B]shore.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Em/B]We shall [G/D]sing [D]on that [D7/C]beautiful [G]shore
[G/B]The melodious songs [Bm]of the blest,
[Em/B]And our spirits [G/D]shall sorrow no [D7/C]more
[C]Not a [G]sigh for the blessing of [D7/C]rest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Em/B]To our [G/D]bountiful [D7/C]father [C]above
[G/B]We will offer our [Bm]tribute of [D]praise;
[Em/B]For the glorious [G/B]gift of His [D7/C]love
[C]And the [G]blessings that hallow our [D7/C]days.
{end_of_verse}
